2026-07-24 (evening) — IMPLEMENTATION PASS ON WO 326-332
================================================================================
Deploy state: client REBUILT (dist-web current) — NEEDS KIOSK RELOAD to see the client
fixes. Node service restarted (WO-329 live). Caspar playout untouched.

✅ 326  BOTH your symptoms were real client bugs, fixed + committed:
        - "aspect locked always": the W/H inputs paired each other from a STALE captured
          layer object — after unlocking, the UI kept showing locked-aspect numbers the
          model never had. Pairing now happens only in patchFillPx (fresh state, content
          aspect) and the inputs re-sync from the model after every change.
        - "W/H has no effect on pgm": the inspector-edit path never armed the mixer
          nudge, and in edit-on-PGM mode geometry-only edits early-return with "the PGM
          nudge owns it" — so inspector geometry edits reached NOTHING on air (canvas
          drags worked; that's why it felt arbitrary). Both paths arm the nudge now.
        NOTE: in NORMAL editing mode, PGM still only updates on take — live-on-air apply
        remains the edit-on-PGM compose mode, by design. Say if you want that changed.
✅ 327  Borders now use each destination's true resolution (explicit w/h → videoMode →
        1080p); no-layout fallback tiles per-destination cells. KIOSK RELOAD.
✅ 331  Live thumbnails stop refetching every render: TTL-window cache-bust like the deck
        thumbs; explicit capture/upload still force-refresh. KIOSK RELOAD.
✅ 329A Server-issued monotonic rev replaces the wall-clock 409. Verified LIVE on this
        box: no-rev autosave accepted (grace) → rev 1; echo → rev 2; stale echo → 409
        stale_rev. Clock skew can no longer produce bogus "payload is older" errors.
        (Found + deleted a dead duplicate module project-scenes-persist.js on the way —
        first pass patched it and changed nothing; live verify caught it.)
        Part B (two clients editing simultaneously = last-write-wins) still needs your
        Option 1 (edit lock) vs Option 2 (per-section merge) decision — see WO-329.
🟡 332  Root cause found + fixed in repo: evtest block-buffers when piped, the listener
        never saw ANY button events (journal has zero presses ever) — only the firmware
        long-hold hard-off worked. Fix = stdbuf line-buffering (+ a now_ms overflow +
        per-press journal line). NEEDS YOUR SUDO to activate:
          sudo install -m 755 ~/highascg/tools/runtime/highascg-power-button-listen.sh \
            /usr/local/lib/highascg/highascg-power-button-listen.sh
          sudo systemctl restart highascg-power-button.service
        Then: short-press → journal "press" + network reset; hold 3s → clean poweroff.
🟡 330  Audit done: Companion runs module 1.0.1; ALL the WO-170 actions live only in the
        packaged-but-undeployed 1.0.3. Instance pins 1.0.1 in db.sqlite, so the installer
        was upgraded to repoint stale pins safely. NEEDS YOUR SUDO (drops the desk ~30s):
          sudo systemctl stop companion \
            && ~/highascg/tools/eggs/companion/install-companion-module.sh \
            && sudo systemctl start companion
